ctm -catchM\
Catch miss is stroke arc degrees measured from where the blade is fully square just before it moves sternward to where 5% of max bend has developed on the oar. \
\
fnm - finishM\
Finish miss is stroke arc degrees from where the oar bend has dropped to 5% of max bend to where the blade has started to feather. \
\
rat - ratio\
Ratio = stroke duration / drive time.   Specifically drive time is the timing of when the strokeLength is measured and does not include time during CatchMiss and FinishMiss.\
\
mrs - maxRot\
This is the max rotational speed of the oar during the drive.\
\
drv - drivework\
\
This is the work done by the rower during the drive portion of the stroke. \
\
mid - midWork\
The value is a percentage (0-100% - NOT stroke arc degrees) This value is the percentage of stroke length representing the median of work distribution. For example, a value less than 50 represents a front end loaded force distribution.\
